# Frontend workflow — read AGENTS.md

The full workflow (pre-flight checklist, tool priority, risk-flagged
skills, MCP server table) lives in `AGENTS.md` at the project root.
That file is the single source of truth — read it in full before
building or editing any UI component or page.

Do not duplicate its content here; this file exists only so Cursor
auto-attaches the rule when a matching file glob is touched. If you
are editing anything under components/app/pages/ui or any .tsx/.jsx
file, `AGENTS.md`'s checklist applies to this task.

Minimum enforcement, restated for glob-matching reliability:
1. shadcn MCP search before writing any component from scratch.
2. Context7 MCP for current framework/library API docs.
3. Chrome DevTools MCP to visually verify before calling anything done.
4. accessibility + impeccable skills before marking the task complete.

If any of these tools/skills are unavailable when needed, state that
explicitly rather than silently skipping to hand-written code.
